# check: fail error[E13c]: the receiver of 'Format' is a number written as a literal - put it in a variable of the type wanted, or convert it, as in 'I64(7)'
# also: error[E13c]: the receiver of 'Bits' is a number written as a literal
# also: error[E13c]: the receiver of 'Hash' is a number written as a literal
# also: compilation failed with 3 errors
# E13c: parentheses, a minus sign or arithmetic of literals still leave a number written as a literal, with no type of
# its own until it lands - each is refused, once, and the calls still give their results (no error follows from them)
fn main() ? {
    t := (255).Format(16)
    b := (-0.0).Bits()
    h := (1 + 2).Hash()
    assert t == "ff" and b != 0 and h != 0
}
